{
  "info": {
    "name": "LuminaMind - Auth Server",
    "description": "Test cases for the LuminaMind ts-server auth routes: register, login, refresh, logout, me.\n\nHow to use:\n1. Import this collection into Postman.\n2. Set the `baseUrl` collection variable (default http://localhost:3000) to match your server's PORT.\n3. Make sure Postman's cookie jar is enabled (it is by default) so the httpOnly refreshToken cookie is stored and sent automatically between requests.\n4. Run requests top to bottom within a folder for the intended flow, or use the whole collection with the Collection Runner.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "testEmail", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "testPassword", "value": "Str0ng!Passw0rd123", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Register",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register - success (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Generate a unique email each run so re-running the collection doesn't hit 409",
                  "const uniqueEmail = `test.${Date.now()}@luminamind.dev`;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testEmail', uniqueEmail);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has accessToken', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.accessToken).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('refreshToken cookie is set as httpOnly', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('refreshToken')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"{{testPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Registers a brand-new user with a unique, generated email. Expects 201 + accessToken in body + refreshToken httpOnly cookie set."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - duplicate email (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 409', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Error message mentions existing user', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('error');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"{{testPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Re-uses the {{testEmail}} set by the previous request to hit the 'User already exists' path. Run '1. Register - success' first so testEmail is populated."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - passwords don't match (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"mismatch.{{$timestamp}}@luminamind.dev\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng!Passw0rd123\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"Different!Passw0rd456\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Tests the Zod .refine() check — password and confirmPassword deliberately don't match."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - weak password (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"weakpw.{{$timestamp}}@luminamind.dev\",\n  \"password\": \"short\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"short\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Password fails min length + missing uppercase/number/special-character regex checks from registerSchema."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - invalid email format (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"not-an-email\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng!Passw0rd123\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"Str0ng!Passw0rd123\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - extra field rejected by strictObject (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"strict.{{$timestamp}}@luminamind.dev\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng!Passw0rd123\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"Str0ng!Passw0rd123\",\n  \"isAdmin\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "registerSchema uses z.strictObject — any field not explicitly declared (like isAdmin here) should cause a 400, not be silently ignored. Good regression test if the schema ever changes."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - empty body (400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Tests the 'Request body is missing/invalid' branch of validateBody with a technically-present but empty JSON object."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Login",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login - success (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has accessToken', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('refreshToken cookie is set', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('refreshToken')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in with the same account created in '1. Register - success'. Run that request first (in the same Postman run) so {{testEmail}} is populated."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - wrong password (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"TotallyWrongPassword999!\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - nonexistent email (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Error message does not reveal whether email exists', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.error.toLowerCase()).to.include('credentials');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"no-such-user-{{$timestamp}}@luminamind.dev\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ng!Passw0rd123\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Checks that the error message is identical/generic whether the email doesn't exist or the password is wrong (no user-enumeration leak)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Me",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Me - valid token (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains user with matching email, no password field', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('user');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.user).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Run after Register or Login so {{accessToken}} is populated. Confirms the User schema's select:false on password actually holds even via .lean()."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me - missing token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "No Authorization header at all."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me - malformed token (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer this.is.not.a.valid.jwt" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Garbage token — should hit jwt.verify's failure path, falling into the generic 'Invalid access token' branch (not the TokenExpiredError branch)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me - expired token (401 + WWW-Authenticate header)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('WWW-Authenticate header signals token_expired', function () {",
                  "    const header = pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate');",
                  "    pm.expect(header).to.include('token_expired');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{expiredAccessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "IMPORTANT: {{expiredAccessToken}} is not auto-generated. To test this: 1) temporarily set ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL to a tiny value like 5 (seconds) in your .env, 2) log in, 3) wait past the TTL, 4) paste that now-expired token as the 'expiredAccessToken' collection variable, then run this request. This is exactly the case your fetchInterceptor's refresh-trigger logic depends on — confirming the WWW-Authenticate header actually appears is the single most important test in this collection for the client integration to work."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Refresh",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Refresh - success (200), rotates cookie",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has a NEW accessToken', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.accessToken).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken'));",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('refreshToken cookie is rotated (still present)', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('refreshToken')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Relies on Postman's cookie jar sending the refreshToken cookie automatically (set during Register/Login). No body needed."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh - old refresh token reused after rotation (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "refreshToken={{staleRefreshToken}}",
                "description": "Manually paste a refresh token value that was already rotated out (e.g. copy the cookie value BEFORE running 'Refresh - success' above, then run this after)."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Regression test for refresh-token rotation: a refresh token that was already consumed/rotated must NOT work a second time. This directly tests the concurrent-refresh race scenario discussed for the web client — if this ever returns 200, rotation is broken."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh - no cookie present (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Cookie", "value": "", "disabled": false }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Run this in a fresh incognito-style request (clear cookies for this domain first, e.g. via Postman's Cookies manager) to simulate no refreshToken cookie at all."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Logout",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Logout - success (200), clears cookie",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has success message', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('message');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh after logout should now fail (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "IMPORTANT regression check: run this immediately after 'Logout - success'. It confirms the refresh token was actually deleted from the DB by logout, not just that the cookie was cleared client-side. If this returns 200 instead of 401, logout isn't cleaning up the DB record."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Full happy-path flow (run in order)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Full flow - see folders 1-5",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Placeholder request. Suggested order for a full manual or Collection-Runner pass:\n1. 1. Register > Register - success\n2. 3. Me > Me - valid token\n3. 4. Refresh > Refresh - success\n4. 3. Me > Me - valid token (again, confirms new token works)\n5. 5. Logout > Logout - success\n6. 5. Logout > Refresh after logout should now fail\n\nUse the Collection Runner with only these six requests selected, in this order, for a one-click end-to-end smoke test."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
